Skip source-checkout-only CLI install and teleop tests on installed packages.

Several cli/ unit tests load the repository root pyproject.toml or run a script
from the source scripts/ directory, so they only work from a source checkout:

  - TestCommandInstallDispatch and TestEnsureCudaTorch exercise install paths
    that always read dependency pins from the root pyproject.
  - TestEnsureNewton.test_installs_pinned_release_when_absent and the two
    TestInstallRootExtraExcludesIsaacSim tests read dependency metadata from it.
  - test_teleop_workflow_help_exposes_task_preset_selectors executes scripts
    from the source scripts/ directory.

Gate them through the existing source_checkout_root fixture. The teleop test
also resolves its script from the returned checkout root, matching the
surrounding upstream tests.
